Local modifications:
  - dkms.conf: adds PATCH[0..2]/PATCH_MATCH[0..2] to apply the local hardening
    patches (see below) during the DKMS build. DKMS 3.2.2 resolves the
    PATCH[] value below its patches/ directory.
  - patches/0001-t2gmux-bounded-drain.patch: bound the interrupt acknowledge
    loop in gmux_interrupt_work() to 32 drains; if the status does not
    clear, disable the interrupt source via gmux_stop_interrupts() and bail
    out so suspend/shutdown/unload do not block forever on power_lock.
  - patches/0002-t2gmux-pm-quiesce.patch: introduce gmux_data->quiescing;
    set it under power_lock in gmux_suspend()/gmux_shutdown(), have the
    interrupt worker refuse to touch the mailbox when set, cancel_work_sync
    the worker, and clear it on gmux_resume().  Prevents a worker queued
    before the suspend path from accessing the mailbox or re-enabling gmux
    interrupts after they were stopped.
  - patches/0003-t2gmux-error-recording.patch: add gmux_data->last_mmio_error
    so the MMIO accessors record -EBUSY/-ETIMEDOUT instead of silently
    returning the historical 0xef sentinel.  Plain callers still receive the
    sentinel for back-compat; the power-state path resets the field before
    each transition so a stale value from a previous transition cannot be
    misread.  Full error-return propagation across all 42 call sites is a
    larger surgery and is documented in the report as future work.

